.Dd $Mdocdate: November 24 2026 $
.Dt ANSILOVE_ERROR 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ansilove_error
.Nd Return an error string
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In ansilove.h
.Ft char *
.Fn ansilove_error "struct ansilove_ctx *ctx"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn ansilove_error
function returns a description of the error code stored in
.Va ctx->error .
The returned string must not be modified or freed.
Successful operations do not generally clear a previous error code.
Check each function's return value before consulting this function.
.Pp
The following error codes are defined in
.In ansilove.h :
.Bl -tag -width ANSILOVE_FILE_WRITE_ERROR
.It Dv ANSILOVE_INVALID_PARAM
A required pointer argument is
.Dv NULL .
.It Dv ANSILOVE_FORMAT_ERROR
The input is empty, malformed, or invalid for the selected renderer.
.It Dv ANSILOVE_MEMORY_ERROR
Memory allocation or input file mapping failed.
.It Dv ANSILOVE_RANGE_ERROR
A value is outside the supported range.
.It Dv ANSILOVE_FILE_READ_ERROR
Opening the input file or obtaining its status failed.
.It Dv ANSILOVE_FILE_WRITE_ERROR
Opening, writing, or closing the output file failed.
.It Dv ANSILOVE_GD_ERROR
A GD image operation or PNG encoding failed.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn ansilove_error
function returns an error string, or
.Dv NULL
if
.Fa ctx
is
.Dv NULL
or its error code is zero or unrecognized.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ansilove_clean 3 ,
.Xr ansilove_init 3 ,
.Xr ansilove_loadfile 3 ,
.Xr ansilove_savefile 3 ,
.Xr libansilove 3
